From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:30:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] process: run a CEF browser's network and video capture in its
 process

Decision 0111 (the owner's choice for PLA-378) amends 0109's switch set:
a CEF browser also gets
--enable-features=NetworkServiceInProcess2,RunVideoCaptureServiceInBrowserProcess,
which Chromium 143 reads to run its network service and its video capture
service in the browser rather than in two utility processes. The
Rockstar Games Launcher's Open on the phone filled the 896 MiB JIT pool
with each child process's builtin copies and FEX code (13 processes, the
network service alone 96 MiB of code). Under desktop Proton the same
Social Club build runs 6 Chromium processes instead of 8 and still shows
its sign-in page.

The storage service has no switch. Social Club gives its children its own
--disable-features value, so AudioServiceOutOfProcess cannot be turned
off this way. --renderer-process-limit=1 has no effect while each site has
its own renderer. None of these is added. The scope is 0109's: only a
browser, and an --enable-features the app passes is kept as it wrote it.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-16-cef-fewer-processes-phone.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/process_ios.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/process_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/process_ios.c
index caccdfa..51eb559 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/process_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/process_ios.c
@@ -872,9 +872,14 @@ static NTSTATUS alloc_handle_list( const PS_ATTRIBUTE *handles_attr, obj_handle_
  * its IPC wants one renderer per page (Stage R). The children (--type=) are left alone and
  * logged. A switch the command line already names is kept as the app wrote it. The new
  * command line's buffer is never freed (one small block per browser start): the caller owns
- * params, and the old buffer stays the caller's. */
+ * params, and the old buffer stays the caller's. Decision 0111 adds the features that run the
+ * network and video capture services inside the browser, so the tree has two processes fewer
+ * for the JIT pool; Chromium 143 names the first NetworkServiceInProcess2. The storage service
+ * has no such switch, and Social Club replaces a browser's --disable-features, so the audio
+ * service stays a process. */
 static const char * const chromium_switches[] = {
     "--in-process-gpu", "--disable-gpu", "--disable-gpu-compositing", "--js-flags=--jitless",
+    "--enable-features=NetworkServiceInProcess2,RunVideoCaptureServiceInBrowserProcess",
 };
 
